hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3045","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, who narrated to us Abu Dawud, who narrated to us Hammam, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from Uqbah ibn Amir (RA) that he asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about his sister, who had made a vow to walk to the Kaaba. The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"," Allah is in no need of your sister's vow; let her ride"," and let her offer a badanah (a sacrificial camel"," the prescribed expiatory offering for this case) as a ransom.\"""""
